        <p>The life cycle of the duck is similar to that of most birds:</p>
        <ol id="ol_qyq_n3m_q2c">
            <li>Egg</li>
            <li>Hatching</li>
            <li>Duckling</li>
            <li>Juvenile</li>
            <li>Adult</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Ducks have these features:</p>
        <ul id="ul_wlv_djm_q2c">
            <li>webbed feet for swimming.</li>
            <li>Shorter legs than other waterfowl.</li>
            <li>Distinctive bill.<ul id="ul_nxf_3jm_q2c">
                    <li>Wide and flat for filter feeding.</li>
                    <li>Long and narrow for fishing (Mergansers).</li>
                </ul></li>
        </ul>
        <p>These are several types of ducks:</p>
        <sl id="sl_nmc_qjm_q2c">
            <sli>Tree ducks.</sli>
            <sli>Surface-feeding ducks.</sli>
            <sli>Bay ducks</sli>
            <sli class="- topic/sli ">Sea ducks</sli>
